 "notes": "Traced from the designer's side-on sketch, which runs north to south: a wall at each end, a big flat-topped mesa near each end with a steep outer cliff and a long ramp down to the low middle (the north ramp is shorter and steeper, the south one longer and gentler, as drawn). Sixteen smaller mesas of different heights stand around them in half-turn mirror pairs. The ground rolls, dry washes cut across it and boulder fields give cover low down. Built as a terrain map: heights come from the mesas, ground, washes and edge below. x and z are metres from the middle; z runs from the north end (team spawn 1) to the south end (spawn 2). Ramp dir is a compass bearing (0 north, 90 east); width is the ramp's half-angle in degrees.",
